# API Contracts Standard

API responses must have **stable contracts**.

Do not change response shapes casually.

## For every API change

* **Check all consumers** (frontend, game-engine, mobile/PWA, scripts)
* **Preserve backward compatibility** when possible
* Return **consistent error shapes**
* Include **enough fields for recovery / debugging**
* **Avoid returning partial critical snapshots**

## Critical snapshot APIs

Must return **complete, self-consistent** data (rooms, live game, wallet, tournament, etc.).

Partial or stale mixes of fields force clients to guess — prefer one authoritative read (see `.cursor/rules/data-access.mdc`).

## Before completing an API change

List consumers affected, document breaking changes if any, and confirm error responses match existing patterns.
